# PR and Communications Executive

### We are recruiting a PR & Communications Executive to join our Marketing and Business Development department on a permanent basis.

## About Macfarlanes

We are a distinctive London-based law firm with a unique combination of services built and shaped around the needs of our clients. Our unrivalled blend of expertise, agility and culture means we have the flexibility to meet their most challenging demands and adapt to the changing world around us. While many of our services can be found at other firms, the mix cannot.

We find, recruit and train talented people from all backgrounds, building careers for the long term, to one day shape and lead the firm. We know each other personally which means we work together with more cohesion, and less formality. Our culture is thoughtful, challenging and supportive, and we are a place where everyone, at whatever level, can thrive. We remain focused on equal treatment in recruitment, retention and promotion.

## What this means for you

Joining Macfarlanes means being part of a collaborative, approachable team who want you to succeed. You'll be encouraged to get involved and recognised for your contribution.

We take your development seriously. Our learning and development programmes are second to none and are designed to help you strengthen your skills.

Above all, you'll be part of a firm where we all work together as part of a cohesive and supportive team, value your efforts and help you to thrive.

## The team

The PR & Communications Executive sits within the firm's Marketing and Business Development department. The individual will report into the Senior PR & Communications Manager who works directly with the Chief Marketing & Business Development Officer.

## The role

The individual will be required to carry out a broad range of good quality work. Key duties will include:

* monitoring legal, business and financial news, applying sound editorial judgement to identify opportunities for profile raising to support the firm's practice, sector and business development priorities;
* working directly with lawyers and business development colleagues to independently develop and execute proactive media campaigns by pitching comment opportunities, by-lined articles, interviews and background briefings and other media opportunities to trade, national and legal press;
* drafting press releases, pitches, articles and other communications materials for use with the media, ensuring house style;
* supporting with day-to-day press office activity, acting as a point of contact with journalists and directing incoming media enquiries;
* supporting the Senior PR and Communications Manager with the planning and delivery of firm PR priorities, including campaigns and content programmes;
* building relationships and engaging with key reporters and editors at relevant media outlets. Identifying opportunities to connect those media contacts to partners of the firm;
* co-ordinating interviews and meetings with reporters and lawyers, including preparing briefing notes for lawyers ahead of media engagements, and staffing media interviews;
* complying with, and supporting, PR team admin processes for proper media monitoring, activity reporting, conflict checking, etc;
* building and maintaining media contact lists on our media database;
* building trusted relationships with partners and internal stakeholders, providing practical communications advice and independently managing media opportunities through the full cycle;
* drafting, preparing and executing social media posts for the firm's social media channels;
* exploring and developing ways of working with generative AI tools with the PR team to drive efficiencies; and
* drafting and editing of awards submissions.

This job description encompasses the main duties of the role and is by no means exhaustive. It is anticipated that duties may vary from time to time according to the needs of the practice area.

During the first six months of employment, you may be required to attend the office four days per week to support onboarding, training and collaboration. Your line manager may adjust this requirement based on your progress and business needs.

## The candidate

The successful candidate will ideally possess the following:

* experience in PR and communications in a professional or financial services environment;
* an interest in business, financial and legal news, with the curiosity to understand how market developments create opportunities for the firm's clients and practices;
* excellent oral and written communication skills, being capable of producing quality work product and generating first drafts that require minimal revision, with adapted messages for different audiences;
* strong interpersonal skills, including being a team player in a collaborative organisation;
* be keen to learn and develop;
* excellent organisation skills, including the ability to prioritise and coordinate own work and to multitask efficiently and work under tight deadlines;
* proven ability to deal with complex subject matter, preferably legal;
* strong attention to detail;
* experience using PR tools including PR media database and media monitoring platforms;
* ability to function in a collaborative organisation and be a team player;
* highly motivated and collaborative. Proactive in identifying opportunities, solving problems and driving activity forward independently;
* polite, professional, positive manner; and
* ability to handle sensitive information appropriately.

## Application screening

Any offer of employment with us is subject to our pre-employment checks which are conducted by a third-party screening provider. These may include but are not limited to your professional and academic qualifications, any criminal records and employment references. These checks will be initiated with your consent and your offer will be subject to the successful completion of these checks.

## Our commitment to inclusion

Inclusion is one of our key priorities and it is a goal we are actively working towards. We believe that an inclusive, forward-thinking culture is intrinsically important and enables us to provide innovative solutions to our clients.

We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, bringing different perspectives and experiences, making Macfarlanes an exciting and stimulating place to work. We seek to recruit the best candidates, regardless of age, gender, race, ethnicity, social or economic background, religion, disability, sexual orientation or any other characteristic.

As part of this commitment, we will ask you certain diversity data questions. We would really appreciate you and/or your recruiter completing these questions when submitting an application to Macfarlanes as this data enables us to measure our progress and identify any actions needed to continue to support an inclusive culture. This data is anonymised to maintain the privacy of applicants. If you have any questions relating to how this data is used, please contact a member of the recruitment team.

Should you require any adjustments during the application and/or interview process, please do not hesitate to inform your recruiter or a member of the recruitment team. Please note, the job description is available in other accessible formats (for example, large print).

We are a Disability Confident Employer and will offer an interview to disabled applicants who best meet the essential criteria for the role. If you would like to apply through the Disability Confident Interview Scheme, please email the recruitment team at recruitment@macfarlanes.com.

## Responsible business

From pro bono work to mentoring and sustainability, we focus on what matters. We use our skills and resources to make a positive difference, for our clients, our people and our communities.

**Job title:** Regional Manager - Ireland

**Location:** Field based – Northern Ireland

We are looking for a Regional Manager to cover both the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, based in one of those locations. **Please apply for this position only if you are available/interested in being based in the Northern Ireland location.**

**Why Join HSB?**

We don’t just inspect—we protect. At HSB, you’ll join a team with a clear purpose, strong values, and a supportive culture where your expertise is respected and your contributions matter. From flexible working to wellbeing support, we invest in you so you can bring your best self to work—every day.

Apply today and become part of a company that doesn’t just engineer safety—but inspires trust.

**What You’ll Be Doing**

As a Regional Manager, you will lead a team of Engineering Surveyors across the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, ensuring the delivery of exceptional customer service, operational excellence, and regulatory compliance. You'll work closely with Operations Managers and Technical Teams to ensure contractual commitments are achieved while creating an engaged, motivated, and high-performing workforce. You will be responsible for resource planning, performance management, recruitment activities, customer satisfaction, financial performance, and maintaining the highest standards of safety and service delivery within your region.

**What Makes This Role Special**

* Leadership impact: Lead and inspire a team of engineering professionals who make a difference every day;
* Business ownership: Take full responsibility for the operational and financial performance of your region, including P&L accountability;
* Growth opportunity: Play a key role in supporting business growth ambitions across Ireland while developing your own career;
* Field-based leadership: Work closely with your team in the field, providing coaching, support, and visible leadership;
* Trusted brand: Join a business recognised for technical excellence, customer service, and innovation as part of the wider Munich Re Group.

**What You Bring**

* Proven leadership experience managing field-based engineering or service delivery teams;
* Strong people management skills with the ability to motivate, coach, and develop high-performing teams;
* Excellent stakeholder and customer relationship management capabilities;
* Strong commercial awareness with experience managing budgets, performance metrics, and business objectives;
* Excellent planning and organisational skills, with the ability to effectively balance resources and workloads;
* A confident and proactive approach with a strong focus on results and continuous improvement;
* Commitment to maintaining and promoting a positive safety culture.

**What You’ll Need**

* Demonstrable experience leading field-based engineering or service-oriented teams;
* Engineering qualification;
* GCSE Maths and English (or equivalent);
* Strong understanding of KPI management and operational performance delivery;
* Knowledge of regulations including LOLER, PSSR, PUWER, COSHH, and Safety, Health and Welfare at Work Regulations would be advantageous;
* Previous experience within engineering inspection, lifting equipment, pressure systems, LEV systems, power presses, or related engineering disciplines would be advantageous;
* Holder of a full UK or Irish driving licence with no more than 6 penalty points.

**What We Offer**

In addition to a competitive salary and excellent work-life balance, you'll benefit from an industry-leading rewards package:

* 25 days Annual Leave + Bank Holidays + 2 Well-being days each year
* Ability to buy or sell leave.
* Up to 13% Pension contribution (9% non-contributory plus up to 4% matching contribution).
* Eligibility for an Annual Bonus up to 15% (dependent on Group performance)
* Private Medical & Dental (options to add family members at discounted rates)
* Life Assurance of six times salary
* Wellbeing and Development Scheme + EAP + Health Assessments (subject to scheme eligibility)
* Study & continuing Professional Development Support
* Choice of company vehicle or car allowance
* Access to Salary Sacrifice Car scheme
* Access to a range of discounted benefits such as critical illness cover and mortgage advisory services.

**Diversity, Equity & Inclusion**

At HSB, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion foster innovation and resilience and enable us to act braver and better. Embracing the power of DEI is at the core of who we are. We recognise diversity can be multi-dimensional, intersectional, and complex, so we want to build a diverse workforce that includes a wide range of racial, ethnic, sexual, and gender identities; economic and geographic backgrounds; physical abilities; ages; life, school, and career experiences; and political, religious, and personal beliefs. Additionally, we are committed to building an equitable and inclusive work environment where this diversity is celebrated, valued, and has equitable opportunities to succeed.

All candidates in consideration for any role can request a reasonable adjustment at any point in our recruitment process. You can request an adjustment by speaking to your Talent Acquisition contact.

## **Personal Assistant to the Port Director - part time**

Are you an organised, proactive Personal Assistant who enjoys supporting senior leaders, building strong relationships and using technology to keep things running efficiently?

We are seeking a professional Personal Assistant to providd executive support for our new Port Director at King George V Dock in Glasgow, as well as the wider leadership team. This is a varied role at the heart of a busy port and logistics operation, helping to coordinate meetings, travel, events, stakeholder activity and key business priorities.  This role is a part time role working 25 hours per week, based in the office 5 days per week.

## **Your role**

You will provide high-quality executive support, manage complex diaries, arrange travel, organise internal and external meetings, prepare agendas, collate papers and support reports, presentations and business documents. You will also help manage correspondence, maintain accurate records, raise purchase orders and ensure day-to-day administration is handled efficiently and professionally.

As a trusted point of contact, you will work with colleagues, customers and external partners with discretion, care and attention to detail. You will use sound judgement to balance competing priorities, anticipate what is needed and use digital tools to improve coordination and make processes more efficient.

## **What you'll bring**

You will bring:

* PA, executive assistant or senior administrative experience in a busy organisation, ideally operating at scale and pace;
* Confidence supporting senior stakeholders, managing confidential information and coordinating a range of priorities;
* Effective organisation, adaptability and the ability to prioritise while keeping a calm, customer-focused approach;
* Clear communication skills and the ability to build effective relationships across the business;
* Good Microsoft Office skills, including Outlook, Word and PowerPoint, with confidence using technology to plan, organise and communicate;
* Experience preparing papers, agendas, minutes, reports or presentations, and arranging travel, meetings or events.
* Discretion, attention to detail, a positive approach and the ability to contribute in a busy port environment.

## **Who are we?**

You will bring:

* PA, executive assistant or senior administrative experience in a busy organisation, ideally operating at scale and pace;
* Confidence supporting senior stakeholders, managing confidential information and coordinating a range of priorities;
* Effective organisation, resilience and the ability to prioritise while keeping a calm, customer-focused approach;
* Clear communication skills and the ability to build effective relationships across the business;
* Good Microsoft Office skills, including Outlook, Word and PowerPoint, with confidence using technology to plan, organise and communicate;
* Experience preparing papers, agendas, minutes, reports or presentations, and arranging travel, meetings or events.
* Discretion, attention to detail, a positive approach and the ability to contribute in a busy port environment.

## **What we can offer you**

In addition to a competitive salary, we have a strong track record of developing our people to expand their skills and experience and develop their careers.  Valuing and rewarding our workforce is important to us which is why we offer a fantastic range of flexible benefits to choose from, such as:

* 27 days holiday per annum (plus bank holidays)
* Matched Contribution Pension Scheme up to 10%
* Peel Ports Flexible Benefits including salary sacrifice car scheme, healthcare cash plans, Cycle2Work Scheme, critical illness insurance, gyms, retail vouchers
* Commitment to learning and personal development
* We promote good physical and mental health and can provide additional support to colleagues via our employee assistance programme when required

If you believe you have the skills and experience we are seeking and you want to join a thriving and ambitious place to work, we’d really like to hear from you!

**About the role:**

PwC UK Healthcare Corporate Finance team are sector specialists advising privately owned, PE backed and large corporate clients across the country. We advise on an exciting variety of transactions on the sell-side and buy-side, with a typical deal size of c.£100-500m+.

As a Healthcare CF team, we have a leading reputation for executing high-profile transactions, advising on some fantastic deals nationally and internationally across Europe, giving fantastic exposure to a variety of deal structures and clients across the sector.

We’re looking for a confident, collaborative Manager who brings 2-4 years of deal experience, a proactive mindset, and commercial acumen. Knowledge and understanding of the applicable regional dynamics (economic, political, industry-focussed) is preferred but not essential. In return, you’ll work within a motivated team of dealmakers, helping clients navigate exciting, complex and fast-paced transactions.

**What your days will look like:**

As a Manager, you’ll bring technical expertise, commercial insight, and leadership, to help clients through the complexities of dealmaking.

Your day-to-day will include:

* Supporting live transactions end-to-end, from origination and marketing through to execution and completion, with ownership over key workstreams;
* Building trusted client relationships and delivering high quality work, across pitch documents, marketing materials, financial analysis and other transaction deliverables;
* Getting involved in our origination efforts; conducting detailed market, financial and commercial research, supporting with proposals, and meeting with potential targets;
* Supporting and coaching junior team members, fostering a collaborative and high-performing team environment.

**This role is for you if:**

* You have Corporate Finance experience, with end-to-end deal experience;
* You have strong financial analysis and modelling skills, as well as commercial acumen and the ability to think strategically;
* You have excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to build trusted relationships with clients;
* You have a pro-active mindset, pay strong attention to detail, and can manage multiple workstreams and deadlines in a fast-paced deal environment;
* You can work effectively within multi-disciplinary teams, and work collaboratively with those around you.
* Must possess an ACA/CA/ACCA qualification (or international equivalent) or have equivalent work experience. This includes international candidates who qualify through experience in their home country

**What you’ll receive from us:**

No matter where you may be in your career or personal life, our benefits are designed to add value and support, recognising and rewarding you fairly for your contributions.

We offer a range of benefits including empowered flexibility and a working week split between office, home and client site; private medical cover and 24/7 access to a qualified virtual GP; six volunteering days a year and much more.

Why Deals?



In Deals we solve the important problems that stand in the way of value being created, sustained, realised or protected for our clients – working together to aid responsible recovery and growth. Working on iconic deals with national and global clients, we put together major mergers and acquisitions and resolve business crises - from international take-over bids to financial crime investigations and cases of insolvency. We draw upon our deals experience across many industries to support and partner with our clients, to positively impact society and the communities in which we operate.

# **Senior Cost Control Engineer**

#### Senior Cost Control Engineer

**Company description:**

**Saipem** is a global leader in the engineering and construction of major projects for the energy and infrastructure sectors, both offshore and onshore. Saipem is “One Company” organized into business lines: **Asset Based Services**, **Drilling**, **Energy Carriers**, **Offshore Wind**, **Sustainable Infrastructures**, **Robotics & Industrialized Solutions**. Always oriented towards technological innovation, the company’s purpose is “**Engineering for a sustainable future**”. As such Saipem is committed to supporting its clients on the energy transition pathway towards Net Zero, with increasingly digital means, technologies and processes geared for environmental sustainability. Listed on the Milan Stock Exchange, it is present in more than **50 countries** around the world and employs about **30,000 people of over 130 nationalities**.

**Purpose of the position****:**

We are looking for a **Senior Cost Control Engineer** to join our **Project Control and Project Risk Management** area, with direct responsibility for the economic and financial control of complex, high-value projects.

The selected candidate will be responsible for managing the project cost control system, ensuring accurate cost monitoring, variance analysis, forecast updates and timely support to the Project Manager and Management through reliable and actionable data.

This is a senior-level role requiring solid experience in complex project environments, strong analytical skills, advanced ownership and the ability to interact effectively with Project Managers, Project Control Managers, corporate functions, AFC, Procurement, Contract Management and internal and external stakeholders.

**Here below your responsibilities****:**

* + **Carry out corrosion assessments, identify damage mechanisms and perform corrosion rate calculations**
  + **Advise for equipment, valves, and piping material selection based on internal and external corrosion**
  + **Create and develop Material Selection Diagrams (MSD) and Corrosion Loop Diagrams (CLD)**
  + **Create and develop Corrosion control strategies to cover different corrosion mitigations methodologies**
  + **Define the Integrity Operating Windows (IOW)**
  + **Create and develop the Corrosion Management Program (CMP)**
  + **Support Maintenance and Inspection Team within the RBI assessment process**
  + **Technical support for Root Cause Analysis (RCA) e Failure Analysis**
  + **Technical Support to Management of Change (MOC)**
  + **Quality Assurance: Ensure all project deliverables adhere to the company's QA/QC protocols and ISO standards.**
  + **Execution & Oversight: Execute and supervise engineering tasks using approved company and client methodologies to maintain high quality and project alignment.**
  + **HSE Compliance: Enforce and monitor all Health, Safety, Environmental (HSE) and Quality Management procedures for both the company and clients.**

**Key Responsibilities**

The selected candidate will be responsible for:

* setting up, managing and updating the project cost control system in line with procedures, company standards and contractual requirements;
* defining and maintaining the **Cost Breakdown Structure** and ensuring proper project budget allocation;
* analyzing the Original Control Budget and preparing the Revised Control Budget, highlighting deviations and critical areas;
* monitoring actual costs, committed costs, accruals, physical and economic progress, earned value and value of work done;
* preparing and updating forecast data, including **Estimate at Completion** and **Estimate to Completion**;
* promptly identifying deviations from approved budget and current forecasts, proposing corrective actions and mitigation scenarios;
* supporting the Project Manager in achieving economic, quarterly and yearly targets, including costs, revenues, cash flow and invoicing;
* contributing to change management, claim management and cost impact analysis related to contractual variations;
* supporting the risk and opportunity management process through cost evaluations and scenario analysis;
* preparing periodic project and company reports, including Cost Control Reports, Project Status Reports, cash flow and management analyses;
* collaborating with AFC, Procurement, Contract Management, Planning and other project functions to ensure data consistency, compliance and traceability;
* promoting a cost-conscious culture within the project team, with a proactive approach to economic performance and risk management.

**Candidate Profile**

The ideal candidate has:

* solid experience as Cost Control Engineer, Project Control Engineer or in similar roles within EPC, Oil & Gas, Energy, Engineering, Construction or large industrial project environments;
* proven ability to manage complex budgets, forecasts, cost reporting, cash flow and variance analysis;
* advanced knowledge of project control, cost control, budgeting, forecasting, earned value and reporting processes;
* experience in managing Cost Breakdown Structures, Work Breakdown Structures and related integration with corporate systems;
* familiarity with procurement processes, project accounting, accruals, invoicing, cash-in/cash-out and AFC principles;
* ability to contribute to risk management, change management and contract management processes;
* advanced knowledge of tools such as SAP, PRISM, Primavera P6, advanced Excel and project reporting systems;
* ability to work in international, multidisciplinary and complex environments;
* excellent written and spoken English.

**What else should you know****?** You will have the opportunity to travel abroad based on the projects you will work for and within the [projects scope] assigned.

**What can we offer to you:**

* [Permanent Contract/Fixed term]

* **Corporate Benefits**: We offer a comprehensive benefits package.
* **Hybrid working model****:** [*if applicable*] NA
* Our **One Saipem Way** soft skills model leverages on skills development, career growth, opportunities to innovate through complex challenges by promoting communication and collaboration to achieve common goals.
